# Read by CUPS's stock usb backend (every file in /usr/share/cups/usb/ is loaded).
#
# `blacklist` makes the stock backend ignore a printer, so Settings > Printers lists it only once, through
# the rstationlp backend (which uses the kernel's usblp node and never the USB control endpoint).
# The SATO WS408 stops answering control requests ~100 s after it enumerates on a Pi 4, which leaves the
# stock backend unable to identify it ("usb://Unknown/Printer"). Keep this in step with PRINTERS in rstationlp.
#
# vendor   product  quirk
0x0828 0xa003 blacklist
